      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 19:28",
        "textualBasisJa": "When they heard this they were filled with anger, and cried out, saying, “Great is Artemis of the Ephesians!”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 19:34",
        "textualBasisJa": "But when they perceived that he was a Jew, all with one voice for a time of about two hours cried out, “Great is Artemis of the Ephesians!”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 19:35",
        "textualBasisJa": "When the town clerk had quieted the multitude, he said, “You men of Ephesus, what man is there who doesn’t know that the city of the Ephesians is temple keeper of the great goddess Artemis, and of the image which fell down from Zeus?"
      }
